        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): accept agents.defaults.compaction.enabled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users setting `agents.defaults.compaction.enabled: false` in `openclaw.json` would get the entire config rejected as invalid (`agents.defaults.compaction: Invalid input`), even though session settings already expose a compaction enabled toggle and docs describe disabling auto-compaction.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd `agents.defaults.compaction.enabled` to the public config contract (type, Zod schema, labels, help) and route `false` through the existing `applyAgentAutoCompactionGuard` path so proactive embedded auto-compaction can be turned off. Overflow recovery, OpenClaw preemptive overflow handling, and manual `/compact` stay available.\n\nRelease-owned `CHANGELOG.md` was intentionally not edited.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can disable proactive auto-compaction via config as a workaround for premature compaction without breaking config load. Manual `/compact` and overflow recovery remain usable.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused tests:\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/agent-settings.test.ts src/config/zod-schema.agent-defaults.test.ts src/config/schema.help.quality.test.ts\n# 101 tests passed (prior local run)\n```\n\nRedacted terminal proof after this fix (config load + guard wiring):\n```text\n=== Real behavior proof: compaction.enabled ===\n1) openclaw config accepts agents.defaults.compaction.enabled=false: true\n   parsed.enabled = false\n2) resolveCompactionEnabled(false) => false\n   resolveCompactionEnabled(unset) => true\n3) applyAgentAutoCompactionGuard(compactionEnabled=false) => { supported: true, disabled: true } calls= [ false ]\n4) Scope note: this disables proactive embedded auto-compaction only; overflow recovery + /compact remain available per docs.\n```\n\nAlso regenerated `docs/.generated/config-baseline.sha256` / `config-baseline.counts.json` after rebase onto current main.\n\nFixes #110065.",
